; Singularity VR mod - settings
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; HookUserPointerDraws - a BISECTION LADDER, not an on/off switch.
;
; Hooking DrawPrimitiveUP / DrawIndexedPrimitiveUP stops the game reaching its
; menus, and three explanations for that have now been wrong (bad vtable slot,
; bad signature, file I/O in the hook). Slot and signature are both since
; confirmed exact against d3d9.h, so the cause is still unknown.
;
; Each level adds back exactly one thing. Launch once per level; whichever level
; FIRST fails to reach the menus names the culprit.
;
;   0 = not hooked at all                    <- known good, safe default
;   1 = hooked, forwards immediately          (does the patch alone break it?)
;   2 = level 1 plus a counter                (does touching our globals break it?)
;   3 = full per-eye treatment                (does the duplication path break it?)
;
; If a level hangs, set it back to 0 and relaunch. No rebuild needed.
;
; Why bother: those draws are how UE3 submits dynamic geometry (particles,
; decals, sprites). They are never split per eye, so a centred one lands on the
; seam between the eye halves and disappears - the suspected cause of the chest
; and similar objects vanishing.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

[Render]
HookUserPointerDraws=0

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; There is deliberately no resolution setting here.
;
; Forcing the D3D9 backbuffer does NOT raise UE3's render resolution - the
; engine sizes its scene targets from its own configured resolution, so
; overriding the backbuffer only desynchronises the two and switches stereo off.
;
; Pass it on the command line instead, which the engine reads into its own
; system settings:
;
;   Singularity.exe -ResX=3840 -ResY=2160 -windowed
;
; -windowed is required because fullscreen clamps to real display modes.
; 4992x2688 is refused; the cap appears to be near 4096.
